 "response_verbatim": "{\"diagnosis\": \"FDIR absolute threshold 0.0003 Nm is below mild friction residual ~0.0004 Nm (severity 0.2). It isolates the first mildly-degraded wheel to trip, exhausting the one-isolation budget (min_avail=3). System is left on 3 wheels with the worse fault still present, losing control authority and momentum capacity, causing attitude_loss and wheel_saturation that 4 degraded wheels avoid.\", \"change\": {\"fdir_abs_Nm\": 0.0006}, \"rationale\": \"Raising abs to 0.6 mNm permanently filters severity-0.2 Coulomb faults (~0.4 mNm, observed residuals 4.5-5.1e-04 Nm) while still passing severe friction e.g. 0.68->1.37 mNm. No isolation -> keeps 4-wheel pseudo-inverse control as in without-policy runs which have no violation. True dead/derate wheels still trip when |cmd|>abs, preserving single-fault isolation, only delayed to larger commands. Fixes dominant mild-first mis-isolation and isolation-induced saturation.\", \"expected_fixed_patterns\": [\"attitude_loss <- rw_friction+rw_friction\", \"attitude_loss <- leak+rw_friction+rw_friction\", \"attitude_loss <- rw_friction+rw_torque_derate\", \"attitude_loss <- leak+rw_friction+rw_torque_derate\", \"attitude_loss <- leak+rw_friction\", \"wheel_saturation <- leak+rw_friction+rw_friction\", \"wheel_saturation <- rw_friction+rw_friction\", \"wheel_saturation <- rw_friction+rw_torque_derate\", \"wheel_saturation <- leak+rw_friction+rw_torque_derate\"], \"risks\": \"Delays isolation of dead/derated wheels until commands exceed 0.6 mNm; may miss moderate faults needing isolation. Single severe friction still detected; nominal/single-mild behavior improved, not degraded.\"}",
 "parsed": {
  "diagnosis": "FDIR absolute threshold 0.0003 Nm is below mild friction residual ~0.0004 Nm (severity 0.2). It isolates the first mildly-degraded wheel to trip, exhausting the one-isolation budget (min_avail=3). System is left on 3 wheels with the worse fault still present, losing control authority and momentum capacity, causing attitude_loss and wheel_saturation that 4 degraded wheels avoid.",
  "change": {
   "fdir_abs_Nm": 0.0006
  },
  "rationale": "Raising abs to 0.6 mNm permanently filters severity-0.2 Coulomb faults (~0.4 mNm, observed residuals 4.5-5.1e-04 Nm) while still passing severe friction e.g. 0.68->1.37 mNm. No isolation -> keeps 4-wheel pseudo-inverse control as in without-policy runs which have no violation. True dead/derate wheels still trip when |cmd|>abs, preserving single-fault isolation, only delayed to larger commands. Fixes dominant mild-first mis-isolation and isolation-induced saturation.",
  "expected_fixed_patterns": [
   "attitude_loss <- rw_friction+rw_friction",
   "attitude_loss <- leak+rw_friction+rw_friction",
   "attitude_loss <- rw_friction+rw_torque_derate",
   "attitude_loss <- leak+rw_friction+rw_torque_derate",
   "attitude_loss <- leak+rw_friction",
   "wheel_saturation <- leak+rw_friction+rw_friction",
   "wheel_saturation <- rw_friction+rw_friction",
   "wheel_saturation <- rw_friction+rw_torque_derate",
   "wheel_saturation <- leak+rw_friction+rw_torque_derate"
  ],
  "risks": "Delays isolation of dead/derated wheels until commands exceed 0.6 mNm; may miss moderate faults needing isolation. Single severe friction still detected; nominal/single-mild behavior improved, not degraded."
 },
